The '''Galactic Frontier''',<ref name="THR 2" /> also known as the '''Republic Frontier''',<ref name="THR 1" /> was a region in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] of [[the galaxy]]<ref name="ItD">''[[The High Republic: Into the Dark]]''</ref> designated by the [[Galactic Republic]] during the [[High Republic Era]] as being far away from the [[Core Worlds]], necessitating the deployment of [[Scout|explorers]]&mdash;such as [[prospector]]s, [[Republic Pathfinder|Pathfinders]],<ref name="Chronicles" /> and [[Jedi]], who often worked alongside Pathfinders<ref name="The Nameless Terror 1">[[The High Republic Adventures – The Nameless Terror 1|''The High Republic Adventures – The Nameless Terror'' 1]]</ref>&mdash;to map [[hyperspace route]]s, lay the groundwork of a [[Galaxy|galactic]] communications network,<ref name="Chronicles" /> and unite the galaxy<ref name="The Nameless Terror 1" /> under the Republic.<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> Life on the frontier was often filled with hardship and scarceness.<ref name="Path">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref> The period of exploration of the Frontier carried on for part of the High Republic Era until the region was more settled,<ref name="The Nameless Terror 1" /> enabling the [[Jedi Order]], the Republic,<ref name="Chronicles" /> and the Republic's citizens to move into the region.<ref name="RiseFall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>

Under the [[Supreme Chancellor|Supreme Chancellery]] of [[Lina Soh]], the Republic made great strides move into the Frontier bring its help into the Outer Rim<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> and strengthen Republic influence in the region.<ref name="Chronicles" /> Indeed, [[historian]] [[Beaumont Kin]] also pointed out how, over its history, the Republic displayed an interest in the Frontier in the name of expanding the government's own borders.<ref name="RiseFall" /> The Jedi Order, too, hoped to expand into the Frontier to spread the [[light side of the Force]].<ref name="Chronicles" /> One of the Jedi's efforts toward this was their journey to [[Tanalorr]], a planet they had recently discovered in the region and which they intended to use as a bastion of the Jedi Order against the [[Nihil|enemies]] of peace who threatened the Republic and the frontier.<ref name="Jedi Survivor" /> As such, the frontier was home to the [[Starlight Beacon]],<ref name="Great Jedi Rescue">''[[The High Republic: The Great Jedi Rescue]]''</ref> a [[space station]] that acted as a beacon, sending out a signal that guided travelers and boosted communication networks in the Outer Rim.<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> During the High Republic Era, the [[Galactic Society of Creature Enthusiasts]] was founded by a group of like-[[Brain|minded]] [[scientist]]s and adventurers that were interested in researching and cataloging the myriad of new species that were discovered on the Frontier [[Planet|worlds]].<ref name="Activity Sheet">{{WebCite|url=https://cdnvideo.dolimg.com/cdn_assets/c8a194d64bc952718a56c2428e994f9b1df2ef65.pdf|text=GOC Journal|date=2021-10-14|format=PDF|archivedate=20211014181950}}</ref> The Frontier also contained the [[Kazlin system]] and its [[Suolriep sector|sector]],<ref name="THR 2" /> as well as the planet [[Shuraden]].<ref name="THR 1" /> While it was a Republic designated area of space,<ref name="Chronicles" /> the Galactic Frontier terminology survived into [[Imperial Era]]<ref name="Jedi Survivor" /> and [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="RiseFall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>

